  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider a grid with HHH rows (numbered 111 through HHH) and WWW columns (numbered 111 through WWW). Let's denote the value in a cell in row iii and column jjj by hi,jh_{i,j}hi,j​. NNN particles (numbered 111 through NNN) are distributed in the cells in such a way that there is at most one particle in each cell. For each valid iii, the iii-th particle has a value pip_ipi​ and it is placed in the cell in row yiy_iyi​ and column xix_ixi​.\n\nLet's denote the set of all particles by PPP and the set of all unordered pairs of particles that are located in side-adjacent cells by EEE. We define the value of the grid as\r\nV=∑i∈Ppi⋅hyi,xi+∑(i,j)∈Epi⋅pj .V = \\sum_{i \\in P} p_i \\cdot h_{y_i,x_i} + \\sum_{(i,j) \\in E} p_i \\cdot p_j \\,.V=∑i∈P​pi​⋅hyi​,xi​​+∑(i,j)∈E​pi​⋅pj​.\n\nYou are given the grid and the locations of all particles, but not their exact values ― only ∣p1∣,∣p2∣,…,∣pN∣\\lvert p_1 \\rvert, \\lvert p_2 \\rvert, \\ldots, \\lvert p_N \\rvert∣p1​∣,∣p2​∣,…,∣pN​∣. Your task is to choose the sign of each value pip_ipi​ in such a way that the value VVV is maximum possible. Each sign may be chosen independently from all other signs.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤H,W≤1,0001 \\le H, W \\le 1,0001≤H,W≤1,000",
      "1≤N≤2001 \\le N \\le 2001≤N≤200",
      "∣hi,j∣≤1,000\\lvert h_{i,j} \\rvert \\le 1,000∣hi,j​∣≤1,000 for each valid i,ji, ji,j",
      "1≤yi≤H1 \\le y_i \\le H1≤yi​≤H for each valid iii",
      "1≤xi≤W1 \\le x_i \\le W1≤xi​≤W for each valid iii",
      "∣pi∣≤100\\lvert p_i \\rvert \\le 100∣pi​∣≤100 for each valid iii",
      "no two particles are located in the same cell",
      "the sum of H⋅WH \\cdot WH⋅W over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** N≤15N \\le 15N≤15",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** H≤2H \\le 2H≤2"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers HHH, WWW and NNN.\nHHH lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains WWW space-separated integers hi,1,hi,2,…,hi,Wh_{i,1}, h_{i,2}, \\ldots, h_{i,W}hi,1​,hi,2​,…,hi,W​.\nNNN more lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains three space-separated integers yiy_iyi​, xix_ixi​ and ∣pi∣\\lvert p_i \\rvert∣pi​∣.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print two lines.\n\n\nThe first of these lines should contain a single integer ― the maximum value of VVV.\nThe second line should contain NNN space-separated integers. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these integers should be 111 if you choose a positive sign for the value of the iii-th particle (i.e. its value should be ∣pi∣\\lvert p_i \\rvert∣pi​∣) or −1-1−1 if you choose a negative sign (i.e. its value should be −∣pi∣-\\lvert p_i \\rvert−∣pi​∣).\nIf there are multiple solutions, you may find any one.",
